{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Maximum security deposit and annual deposit increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not collect a security deposit larger than one and one-half times one month's rent, and any yearly increase of the deposit may not exceed 10% of the current deposit.","key_value":"1.5 months' rent; yearly deposit increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey where a landlord chooses to collect a security deposit; prepaid rent held to secure future rent counts as part of the deposit.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Collecting a deposit is optional for the landlord"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2 ). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.78,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Placement of security deposit and tenant's interest","requirement":"A landlord who receives deposit money for ten or fewer units must place it in an insured New Jersey bank or savings and loan in an interest-bearing account; the interest belongs to the tenant and is paid or credited each year.","key_value":"10 or fewer units: insured NJ interest-bearing account","coverage_conditions":"Security deposits for residential rentals in New Jersey; seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days by a person with a permanent residence elsewhere is excluded.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Seasonal use or rental of 125 consecutive days or less is excluded"},"exemptions":"Security deposits for seasonal use or rental of not more than 125 consecutive days for residential purposes by a person whose permanent residence is elsewhere.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"A landlord or designee who receives security deposit money for ten or less units must deposit that money in an insured bank or savings and loan association located in New Jersey in an interest-bearing account at the current interest rate at the time of deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deposit account notice and tenant's right to apply deposit to rent","requirement":"A landlord must tell the tenant in writing within 30 days where the deposit is held and its amount and rate; if notice or interest is not given, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest to rent after allowing 30 days to comply.","key_value":"7% per annum","coverage_conditions":"Tenants whose landlord fails to give the required notice of the deposit account or fails to pay the annual interest as required.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may apply the security money plus 7% interest to rent; if it is applied, the landlord may not demand a further security deposit.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"If a tenant does not receive proper notice or is not paid interest as required, the tenant may use the security deposit for payment of rent by giving the landlord written notice that the security money plus interest at the rate of 7% per annum be applied to rent payments or payments due or to become due from the tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return within 30 days and double-damage remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends the landlord must return the deposit plus interest less itemized deductions, and within five business days after a tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation.","key_value":"30 days; 5 business days after displacement","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; deductions are allowed for damages beyond normal wear and tear and other money owed under the lease.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Tenant may sue for double the amount wrongfully withheld, together with court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant ( N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the deposit and any interest available to the tenant or agent within 15 business days and tell the tenant within three business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who terminate a lease under the Safe Housing Act because of domestic violence; the law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Termination of lease under the Safe Housing Act for domestic violence"},"exemptions":"This law does not apply to transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
